---
import CapturedScreen from './CapturedScreen.astro';
import catchDetails from '../../docs/CID-WEB-CRO-07/captures/catch-details-no-photo-1080x2340.png';

---
<section class="journal-section" id="journal">
<div class="wrap journal-layout">
<figure class="journal-record">
<span class="figure-heading">ONE CATCH, REMEMBERED</span>
<CapturedScreen src={catchDetails} alt="Actual read-only Catch details excerpt for a controlled Brown Trout record without a photo: User entered, Riverside, Dry fly, 0.75 kg, 34 cm, personal notes and Edit catch." />
<figcaption>Actual CatchID UI · Controlled demonstration data · No photo required<br><span>Catch details · saved record excerpt</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="section-copy">
<p class="eyebrow">02 / YOUR CATCH JOURNAL</p>
<h2>Not just a fish.<br>
<em>A day remembered.</em>
</h2>
<p>The place. The moment. The details that would otherwise slip away.</p>
<p>Bring your catches together in a personal history you can return to, catch after catch.</p>
<div class="journal-caption">
<span class="small-rule">
</span>
<p>A place, a method and a note to remember.<br>A saved catch, with no photo required.</p>
</div>
<a class="text-link" href="/fishing-journal-app/">Explore the fishing journal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</a>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<style>
  .journal-record { max-width: 390px; }
  .journal-record > figcaption { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 16px; }
  .journal-record > figcaption span { display: inline-block; margin-top: 4px; }
  @media (min-width: 761px) and (max-width: 900px) {
    .journal-layout { display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; gap: 34px; }
    .section-copy { width: 100%; max-width: 560px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .journal-record { width: calc(100% + 16px); align-self: center; margin-inline: 0; }
  }
</style>
